    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d586-a1">

                <pb facs="0725" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg617"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 49.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Alden to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Board of Commissioners for Foreign
                                Missions,<lb/>Congregational House, Somerset Street</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Boston</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1893-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March 2,
                                1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: The inclosed extracts from
                    correspondence from our imperiled missionaries at Marsovan, Turkey, just
                    received, I send you in addition to documents sent you two or three days ago. We
                    regard them as of very great importance, and you will see that our missionaries
                    have notified the Government that they should appeal to the U. S. embassy. We
                    are sure that you will do everything possible to secure prompt action in this
                    matter.</p>
                <p>Truly, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. K. Alden.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
